From 0bf78bc04d57dbc19831fb09ccbd64285f3b3b4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:33:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: leave the AP 4-way handshake to the host on
 BCM4364

The BCM4364 firmware lists "idauth" in its capabilities, so brcmfmac
enables BRCMF_FEAT_FWAUTH and advertises
NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_4WAY_HANDSHAKE_AP_PSK. hostapd and wpa_supplicant
then pass the PSK to the driver and leave the AP side of the 4-way
handshake to the firmware. On the BCM4364 that handshake never
completes. The client associates, no EAPOL-Key frame is sent, and the
firmware removes the station after about 8 s.

Measured on a MacBookPro15,1 (BCM4364/3, firmware 9.30.514.0.32.5.94,
FWID 01-47278712) with a WPA2-PSK access point and a Samsung Galaxy
S22 Ultra as client:

  offload advertised:  NEW_STATION, DEL_STATION 7.8 s later, no EAPOL
  offload not advertised: 4-way handshake by wpa_supplicant completes,
                          AP-STA-CONNECTED, DHCP lease, traffic flows

Clear BRCMF_FEAT_FWAUTH on the BCM4364 so the host runs the handshake.

Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/feature.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/feature.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/feature.c
index 488364e..255cec3 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/feature.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/feature.c
@@ -318,6 +318,13 @@ void brcmf_feat_attach(struct brcmf_pub *drvr)
 					BIT(BRCMF_FEAT_WOWL_GTK);
 		}
 	}
+	/* The BCM4364 firmware lists "idauth", but in AP mode its
+	 * authenticator never completes the 4-way handshake and the station
+	 * is dropped after about 8 s. Leave the handshake to the host.
+	 */
+	if (drvr->bus_if->chip == BRCM_CC_4364_CHIP_ID)
+		ifp->drvr->feat_flags &= ~BIT(BRCMF_FEAT_FWAUTH);
+
 	/* MBSS does not work for all chips */
 	switch (drvr->bus_if->chip) {
 	case BRCM_CC_4330_CHIP_ID:
-- 
